; HALLOWEEN2026.SCR — "The Last Lantern of Fayd" (Halloween 2026 story event)
; =============================================================================
; Story, clues and treasure of Marren Vey: see original/halloween.txt. GM
; procedure: original/HALLOWEEN_RUNBOOK.md.
;
; REQUIRES FESTITEMS.SCR (permanent, in LEGENDS.CFG: vocabulary + every
; keepsake players carry away) and FALLFEST.SCR loaded FIRST (festival fixtures,
; refreshments). This file redefines room 287 (festival lot + story triggers)
; and the Old Fayd Cemetery rooms, so it must load AFTER FALLFEST.SCR. Not part
; of LEGENDS.CFG — upload as a GM-panel draft, Activate for the event, Disable after.
;
; The original cemetery already has every landmark the story needs:
;   287  Poor Quarter outside the chained gate  -> the campfire / storytelling
;   300  broken obelisk + vine-choked skull     -> clue 1 (copper strip)
;   309  old Maytan tree                         -> clue 2 (brass key)
;   307  outside the caretaker's ruined house    -> shovel + prybar
;   308  caretaker's house, rusted bed           -> clue 3 (parchment)
;   310  hillock with the mausoleum              -> slab, chest, tokens, graves
; Rooms are copied from FAYDFALL.SCR (autumn) with all original items, exits and
; scripts kept. Changes: story items/scripts added, and MONSTER_GROUP removed
; from 299-310 so ordinary cemetery undead don't spawn on a mixed-level party
; (FALLFEST.SCR's opt-in Halloween spawner is separate — keep HWHAUNT 0 during
; the story).
;
; STORY STAGE — named variable HWLANTERN (GMs can @set it to skip/repair):
;   0  dormant (file loaded, nothing happens)
;   1  ARMED by a GM (@set HWLANTERN 1) just before the story begins
;   2  someone said "...your vigil is done" at the fire: Marren manifested,
;      the obelisk token lies in the ashes. Clue 1 (search skull) is live.
;   3  copper strip found         -> clue 2 (search roots, room 309) live
;   4  brass key found            -> clue 3 (search floor, room 308) live
;   5  parchment found            -> search mausoleum (room 310) live
;   6  slab lifted: chest + bag of 12 funeral tokens revealed
;   7  Marren's name spoken by the chest -> tokens can be returned to graves
;   8  all 12 tokens returned: chest open, rewards claimable (SEARCH CHEST)
; Other variables:
;   HWTOKENS  tokens returned so far (Elira Vey's lantern token must be last)
;   HWSPIRITS 1 once the restless spirits have been raised
;   HWHINT    @set HWHINT 1 -> Marren's lantern drifts toward the next
;             location once (auto-resets to 0)
;   HWFIRE    0 burning, 1 blue, 2 dead, 3 rekindled
; Per player: INTNUM1031 = 2026 once that character has claimed a share.
;
; First finders of each leg (strip, key, parchment, slab) are announced to GMs
; via GMMSG "[Last Lantern] ... FIRST", for handing out the engraved funeral
; rings (INUMBER 9346) with @additem / @give.
;
; ID ranges: NOUNDEF 9300-9303, ADJDEF 9300-9311 and INUMBER 9302-9306,
;            9320-9331, 9344-9346 are in FESTITEMS.SCR. Here: MADJDEF 9300,
;            INUMBER 9300-9301, 9307-9314, 9332-9343, MNUMBER 9300,
;            MACRO 9300-9306, CEVENT 9300.
; =============================================================================

; ── Vocabulary ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Nouns/adjectives and every keepsake players can carry away (clue items, the
; twelve tokens, the necklace/charm/ring rewards) live in the permanent
; FESTITEMS.SCR, so they survive after this file is removed.

MADJDEF	9300	restless

VARIABLE HWLANTERN
VARIABLE HWTOKENS
VARIABLE HWSPIRITS
VARIABLE HWHINT
VARIABLE HWFIRE

; ── Macros ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Bodies are wrapped in an always-true IFVAR so every action parses (see
; FALLFEST.SCR). DUMMY vars are per-command scratch values.

; MACRO 9300: put a funeral token on a gravestone. Caller sets DUMMY1 to the
; archetype of the token that belongs on that stone. Inside a PUT script the
; current item (ARCHNUM, REMOVEITEM -1) is the item being put.
MACRO 9300
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  EQUAL DUMMY2 0
  IFVAR ARCHNUM >= 9320
    IFVAR ARCHNUM <= 9331
      EQUAL DUMMY2 1
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY2 = 0
    ECHO PLAYER That has no place on a grave.
  ELSE
    IFVAR ARCHNUM ! DUMMY1
      ECHO PLAYER You hold the token against the weathered stone, but the symbol carved on it does not match.
    ELSE
      EQUAL DUMMY3 1
      IFVAR HWLANTERN < 7
        EQUAL DUMMY3 0
        ECHO PLAYER The token fits the hollow in the stone, but nothing happens. The cemetery seems to be waiting for someone to speak the keeper's name.
      ENDIF
      IFVAR DUMMY3 = 1
        IFVAR DUMMY1 = 9331
          IFVAR HWTOKENS < 11
            EQUAL DUMMY3 0
            ECHO PLAYER You lay the lantern token against the stone, but the lantern carved there stays cold and dark. It will wait until all the others have been returned.
          ENDIF
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
      IFVAR DUMMY3 = 1
        REMOVEITEM -1
        ECHO PLAYER You press the token into a shallow hollow in the gravestone. It settles into place, and its carved symbol glimmers with a pale golden light before sinking into the weathered stone. From somewhere beneath the earth comes a soft and grateful sigh.
        ECHO OTHERS %N presses a token into a gravestone. It glimmers with pale golden light and sinks into the stone, and from somewhere beneath the earth comes a soft and grateful sigh.
        IFVAR DUMMY1 = 9331
          GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N returned Elira Vey's lantern token. The finale begins.
          CALL 9301
        ELSE
          ADD HWTOKENS 1
          GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N returned a token to its grave.
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9301: the finale, after Elira Vey's token is returned. Runs in room 310
; as a timed sequence (the player who placed the token must stay visible —
; @invis suppresses script echoes).
MACRO 9301
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  EQUAL HWLANTERN 8
  ECHO ALL A warm light blossoms inside the lantern carved upon the stone. Beside the chest, the translucent figure of Marren Vey stands with his head bowed.
  PLREVENT 5
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL You hear metal on metal as the brass key in the chest's lock begins to turn by itself. The lock opens with a loud click, and the chest creaks open.
  OPEN 12
  PLREVENT 5
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL Marren's spectral lantern shines with a warm, golden light.
  PLREVENT 5
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL Marren Vey says, "The dead do not fear being forgotten. We fear being remembered falsely."
  PLREVENT 6
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL Marren Vey says, "Tell them that Marren Vey did not abandon his vigil."
  PLREVENT 5
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL Marren looks out across the countless broken graves. "And tell them I was not alone."
  PLREVENT 6
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL Marren Vey whispers, "Forgive me, Elira. I have kept you waiting long enough."
  PLREVENT 5
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL A second figure appears beside him and gently takes his hand. Together, they fade into the golden light.
  PLREVENT 6
  CONTPLREVENT
  ZAPMON
  ECHO ALL Dozens of faint figures become visible throughout the cemetery. They silently incline their heads toward you before fading, with Marren and Elira, into the darkness.
  PLREVENT 3
  CONTPLREVENT
  ECHO ALL [The chest stands open. SEARCH CHEST to receive your share of Marren Vey's cache.]
ENDIF

; MACRO 9302: the caretaker's hidden compartment (room 308).
MACRO 9302
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  IFVAR HWLANTERN < 4
    ECHO PLAYER You poke through the rusted bedframe and scattered kitchenware but find nothing of interest.
  ELSE
    EQUAL DUMMY1 0
    IFCARRY 9304
      EQUAL DUMMY1 1
    ENDIF
    IFVAR DUMMY1 = 0
      ECHO PLAYER Beneath the remains of the bed, half buried in grit, you find a small iron compartment set into the floor. It is locked fast. You would need a key.
      ECHO OTHERS %N kneels beside the rusted bed and runs %h fingers over something in the floor.
    ELSE
      EQUAL DUMMY2 0
      IFCARRY 9305
        EQUAL DUMMY2 1
      ENDIF
      IFVAR DUMMY2 = 1
        ECHO PLAYER The iron compartment beneath the bed stands open and empty. You already have the parchment.
      ELSE
        ECHO PLAYER Beneath the remains of the bed you find a small iron compartment set into the floor. The tarnished brass key turns stiffly in its lock, and the lid grinds open. Inside lies a piece of blackened parchment, which you take.
        ECHO OTHERS %N fits a brass key into something beneath the rusted bed. There is a grinding of old iron, and %s draws out a piece of blackened parchment.
        NEWITEM -1 9305
        EQUAL ROUNDTIME 5
        IFVAR HWLANTERN = 4
          EQUAL HWLANTERN 5
          GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N found the parchment FIRST (leg 3).
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9303: claim a share of Marren's cache (SEARCH CHEST once it is open).
MACRO 9303
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  IFVAR HWLANTERN < 8
    ECHO PLAYER The iron-bound chest is locked tight. An old brass lock holds it shut.
  ELSE
    IFVAR INTNUM1031 = 2026
      ECHO PLAYER You have already received your share of Marren Vey's cache. Leave the rest for the others.
    ELSE
      EQUAL INTNUM1031 2026
      ECHO PLAYER You reach into Marren Vey's chest. Among the decayed velvet and funeral gifts you find a purse of ancient Faydian crowns, an antique silver necklace bearing the image of Old Fayd, and a tiny lantern charm, cold to the touch.
      ECHO PLAYER [You receive 50 crowns, an antique silver necklace, and a tarnished silver lantern charm.]
      ECHO OTHERS %N reaches into the open chest and takes a share of Marren Vey's cache.
      ADD WEALTH 5000
      NEWITEM -1 9344 ADJ1=851 ADJ2=292
      NEWITEM -1 9345 ADJ1=318 ADJ2=292 VAL2=50 VAL3=113
      GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N claimed a share of the cache.
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9304: lift the granite slab (room 310). Needs a prybar or any shovel.
MACRO 9304
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  EQUAL DUMMY1 0
  IFCARRY 9306
    EQUAL DUMMY1 1
  ENDIF
  IFCARRY 484
    EQUAL DUMMY1 1
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 0
    ECHO PLAYER You strain at the granite slab, but it is far too heavy to lift with your bare hands. If only you had something to pry it up with...
    ECHO OTHERS %N strains at the granite slab, without success.
  ELSE
    REMOVEITEM 11
    NEWITEM 12 9311
    NEWITEM 13 9312
    NEWPUT 13 9320
    NEWPUT 13 9321
    NEWPUT 13 9322
    NEWPUT 13 9323
    NEWPUT 13 9324
    NEWPUT 13 9325
    NEWPUT 13 9326
    NEWPUT 13 9327
    NEWPUT 13 9328
    NEWPUT 13 9329
    NEWPUT 13 9330
    NEWPUT 13 9331
    EQUAL ROUNDTIME 10
    ECHO PLAYER You wedge your tool beneath the edge of the slab and heave. With a grinding groan the granite shifts, tilts, and slides aside, revealing a shallow pit. In it rest an iron-bound chest and an old cloth bag, heavy with funeral tokens.
    ECHO OTHERS %N wedges a tool beneath the granite slab and heaves. With a grinding groan the slab slides aside, revealing an iron-bound chest and an old cloth bag in a shallow pit.
    IFVAR HWLANTERN = 5
      EQUAL HWLANTERN 6
      GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N lifted the slab FIRST. Chest + token bag revealed.
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9305: someone tries to force the chest before the tokens are returned.
MACRO 9305
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  IFVAR HWLANTERN >= 8
    ECHO PLAYER The chest already stands open.
  ELSE
    IFVAR HWSPIRITS = 0
      EQUAL HWSPIRITS 1
      ECHO ALL The ground grows bitterly cold. One by one, pale shapes rise from the graves around the hillock -- the restless dead of Old Fayd. They do not attack, but they gather close around the chest, their hollow eyes fixed on you.
      GENMON 9300
      GENMON 9300
      GENMON 9300
      GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N tried to force the chest. Restless spirits raised (they leave when the chest opens).
    ELSE
      ECHO PLAYER The restless spirits press closer around the chest, and a whisper like wind through dry leaves fills your ears: "Return what was taken..."
      ECHO OTHERS The restless spirits press closer around %N.
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9306: the brass key at the Maytan tree (room 309).
MACRO 9306
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  IFVAR HWLANTERN < 3
    ECHO PLAYER You poke among the gnarled roots of the Maytan tree but find nothing but dirt and dead leaves.
  ELSE
    EQUAL DUMMY1 0
    IFCARRY 9304
      EQUAL DUMMY1 1
    ENDIF
    IFVAR DUMMY1 = 1
      ECHO PLAYER You search the roots again, but there is nothing more to find. You already have the brass key.
    ELSE
      ECHO PLAYER Digging your fingers into the dark soil between the roots, you uncover a tarnished brass key wrapped in the rotted remains of a leather cord.
      ECHO OTHERS %N digs among the roots of the Maytan tree and uncovers a tarnished brass key.
      NEWITEM -1 9304
      EQUAL ROUNDTIME 5
      IFVAR HWLANTERN = 3
        EQUAL HWLANTERN 4
        GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N found the brass key FIRST (leg 2).
        ECHO ALL As the key is lifted from the earth, the air turns cold. For a heartbeat Marren Vey stands between the graves, his hooded lantern dark.
        PLREVENT 3
        CONTPLREVENT
        ECHO ALL Marren Vey whispers, "A keeper without a home. A sleeper without a bed. Find where I waited for the morning."
        PLREVENT 3
        CONTPLREVENT
        ECHO ALL Then he is gone, and the grey leaves of the Maytan tree go still.
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF

