;
; 309 — the Maytan tree (clue 2). Tree and roots added as searchable scenery.
NUMBER 309
NAME Cemetery, trail
FOREST
DAY_LIGHT
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
An old Maytan tree leans over the trail. Its long feathery leaves have shrivelled to a dry grey and slowly brush the tops of the old cracked grave stones that line both sides of the trail. To the north is some sort of mausoleum atop of small hillock.
*DESCRIPTION_END
ITEM 0 229 ADJ1=9310
ITEM 1 9307
ITEM 9 693
EXIT S 301
EXIT N 310
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 0
The Maytan tree is ancient and gnarled. Its long grey leaves scrape softly across the names on the surrounding gravestones, and its thick roots knot their way down into the graves themselves. The soil around them is unusually dark.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 1
Thick, knotted roots spread out from the base of the Maytan tree and burrow down among the graves. The soil between them is unusually dark, as if it once drank something other than rain.
*DESCRIPTION_END
IFPREVERB SEARCH 0
  CLEARVERB
  CALL 9306
ENDIF
IFPREVERB SEARCH 1
  CLEARVERB
  CALL 9306
ENDIF
IFPREVERB DIG -1
  CLEARVERB
  CALL 9306
ENDIF
;
; 310 — the hillock and mausoleum: slab, chest, tokens, gravestones, finale.
; Original items/scripts kept: arch to the mausoleum (ref 0), the hidden trail
; (ref 2, any SEARCH) and DIG for body parts (ref 1). Story refs: 10 mausoleum,
; 11 slab, 12 chest, 13 bag, 14 gravestones, 20-31 the twelve graves.
NUMBER 310
NAME Cemetary, hillock
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
This vantage point provides an excellent view of the graveyard cramped
between the towering buildings of Fayd. There are hundreds of gravestones
of every shape, size and configuration, most of which have broken or
fallen. The wilderness has retaken much of the land, choking it with
weeds and vines. A small mausoleum is accessible beneath a stone arch.
*DESCRIPTION_END
OUTDOOR_FLOOR
DAY_LIGHT
EXIT S 309
ITEM 0 60  ADJ1=312  VAL2=311
ITEM 9 693
ITEM 10 9309
ITEM 14 9313
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 10
The mausoleum is a squat block of grey granite beneath a carved stone arch. Weeds grow waist-high around its back wall.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 11
A broad slab of granite lies flat in the weeds behind the mausoleum. Its edges are not quite flush with the ground around it.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 12
A sturdy chest of black oak bound with iron straps, its brass lock green with age. A thousand years in the ground have barely marked it.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 13
An old cloth bag, rotten at the seams, heavy with small bronze funeral tokens. Each token bears a different symbol. (GET TOKEN FROM BAG)
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 14
Hundreds of gravestones crowd the slopes of the hillock, most of them broken or fallen. The runes cut into them are unreadable, but here and there a carved symbol has survived the years.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 20
The gravestone of ADREN BELL, carved with a rising sun divided by a vertical line.
"He opened the eastern gate each morning, until the morning that never came."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 21
The gravestone of MYRA SOL, carved with a closed eye shedding a single tear.
"She saw sorrow in every future but her own."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 22
The gravestone of PELLAN ROE, carved with three stalks of wheat bound with cord.
"From barren earth he raised bread enough for strangers."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 23
The gravestone of TORVEN DANE, carved with a hammer resting across a small flame.
"His hands shaped iron. His heart yielded to none."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 24
The gravestone of SERA NOLL, carved with a bird escaping an open cage.
"No wall held her long, and no grave shall hold her forever."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 25
The gravestone of EDRIS AND MARA VANN, carved with two hands clasped beneath a crescent moon.
"Joined in life, found together when the sky fell."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 26
The gravestone of OREN VALE, carved with a five-pointed star above three wavy lines.
"He followed the river beyond every map, yet the river carried him home."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 27
The gravestone of HESSA KORR, carved with a hound seated beneath a full moon.
"Faithful to those she loved; merciless to those who harmed them."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 28
The gravestone of TALVEN MOR, carved with a quill laid across an ornate key.
"Keeper of records, secrets, and one promise he carried into death."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 29
The gravestone of ILYRA FEN, carved with a leafless tree with seven exposed roots.
"She buried seven children and still found kindness for the living."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 30
The gravestone of JORY PELL, carved with the small handprint of a child.
"He lived nine winters and laughed enough for ninety."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 31
The gravestone of ELIRA VEY, carved with an unlit hooded lantern.
"She kept a light for one who came too late."
*DESCRIPTION_END
; --- original FAYDFALL.SCR room 310 scripts (hidden trail, digging) ---
IFNOITEM 2
  IFPREVERB SEARCH -1
    CLEARVERB
    ECHO PLAYER You discover a hidden trail, leading further up the hill!
    ECHO PLAYER [Round: 10 seconds]
    EQUAL ROUNDTIME 10
    NEWITEM 2 76  VAL2=3638
   ENDIF
ENDIF
IFPREVERB DIG -1
  CLEARVERB
  ECHO PLAYER You dig in the loose earth...
  ECHO OTHERS %N digs in the loose earth.
  ECHO PLAYER [Round: 20 seconds]
  EQUAL ROUNDTIME 20
  RANDOM CHASBONES 1 100 0
  MOD CHASBONES 19
  IFITEM 1
    ECHO PLAYER You don't find anything.
  ENDIF
  IFNOITEM 1
    IFVAR CHASBONES < 8
      ECHO PLAYER You don't find anything.
    ENDIF
    IFVAR CHASBONES > 7
      IFVAR CHASBONES < 10
        ECHO PLAYER You dig up a rotting corpse, without head, legs, or arms.
        NEWITEM 1 650  ADJ1=586
      ENDIF
      IFVAR CHASBONES > 9
        IFVAR CHASBONES < 12
          ECHO PLAYER You dig up a rotting head, its decaying face seeming to watch your every move.
          NEWITEM 1 1273  ADJ1=586
        ENDIF
        IFVAR CHASBONES > 11
          IFVAR CHASBONES < 16
            ECHO PLAYER You dig up a rotting arm, about ready to fall apart.
            NEWITEM 1 649  ADJ1=586
          ENDIF
          IFVAR CHASBONES > 15
            ECHO PLAYER You dig up a rotitng leg, whose foot is missing a toe or two.
            NEWITEM 1 527  ADJ1=586
          ENDIF
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF
; --- story: the mausoleum and the slab ---
IFPREVERB SEARCH 10
  CLEARVERB
  IFVAR HWLANTERN < 5
    ECHO PLAYER You circle the mausoleum, pushing through the weeds, but find nothing of interest.
  ELSE
    EQUAL DUMMY1 0
    IFITEM 11
      EQUAL DUMMY1 1
    ENDIF
    IFITEM 12
      EQUAL DUMMY1 1
    ENDIF
    IFVAR DUMMY1 = 1
      ECHO PLAYER There is nothing more to find behind the mausoleum.
    ELSE
      NEWITEM 11 9310
      EQUAL ROUNDTIME 5
      ECHO PLAYER Pushing through the waist-high weeds behind the mausoleum, you find a broad granite slab lying flat in the earth. Its edges are not quite flush with the ground. It looks loose -- but far too heavy to lift by hand.
      ECHO OTHERS %N pushes through the weeds behind the mausoleum and uncovers a broad granite slab.
      GMMSG [Last Lantern] %N found the granite slab FIRST (leg 4).
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF
